    "final_answer": "I now have all the information I need to provide a comprehensive answer.\n\n## Answer\n\nBased on my research from Wikipedia, here are the details about the most recent World Cup:\n\n### The Most Recent World Cup: 2026 FIFA World Cup\n\n- **When**: The final was played on **July 19, 2026** (the tournament itself ran from June to July 2026)\n- **Where**: The tournament was held across **three host countries — Canada, Mexico, and the United States** — making it the first FIFA World Cup with three co-hosts. The final match took place at **MetLife Stadium** in **East Rutherford, New Jersey** (United States).\n- **Winner**: **Spain** defeated defending champion Argentina **1–0** in extra time, earning Spain its second FIFA World Cup title (the first since 2010). The lone goal was scored by **Ferran Torres**, who was named Man of the Match. Argentine goalkeeper Emiliano Martínez recorded 11 saves in the match.\n\n### Additional context\n- This was the 23rd edition of the FIFA Men's World Cup.\n- It was the first World Cup to feature **48 teams** (expanded from 32).\n- Spain became the first nation to hold both the men's and women's World Cup titles simultaneously (the Women's title was won by Spain in 2023).\n- Attendance at the final was 80,663, refereed by Slavko Vinčić of Slovenia.\n- Spain's path to the final: topped Group H, then defeated Austria (R32), Portugal (R16), Belgium (QF), and France (SF).\n- Argentina's path: won Group H, then beat Cape Verde (R32), Egypt (R16), Switzerland (QF), and England (SF).",
